WEBVTT

00:00.000 --> 00:09.000
Today, Web DSH, Web Terminal, and installed managed clients operate in the user's private workspace.

00:09.000 --> 00:19.000
DSH chat does not forward work to another client. The deployed Agent tasks page separates runtime from backend.

00:19.000 --> 00:29.000
Web DSH controls the task. Python SDK, Claude Code, or Deep Agents runs behind that control surface.

00:29.000 --> 00:40.000
Tasks require approval and stream output. The SDK uses a private checkpoint and supports interrupted recovery.

00:40.000 --> 00:50.000
SDK tool interrupts pause for approval. Kubectl has no token or default kubeconfig, so it grants no access alone.

00:50.000 --> 01:00.000
OpenShell stays disabled until all twenty-five gates pass. Model execution and spoken-content review remain.
